    "intro": "Spinach is a quick leafy crop which can be available for much of the year with careful planning, but it needs steady moisture and rich soil to avoid bolting. There are summer and winter forms of true spinach, while New Zealand spinach is a separate, frost-tender plant often grown as a summer substitute in hot weather. Perpetual spinach, or spinach beet, is a type of leaf beet rather than true spinach. Choose the appropriate type for the season and pick tender leaves regularly.",
