    ],
    "intro": "Salsify and scorzonera are closely related, old-fashioned root vegetables usually treated together. They are delicacies rather than staples: the roots are long, thin, tender and rather awkward to lift and clean, so usable yields can be modest. Salsify has creamy-coloured roots and is often called vegetable oyster because of its delicate, oyster-like flavour; scorzonera is similar but black-skinned. Both prefer deep, friable soil and direct sowing, and both can stand most winter weather.",
